 "notes": "Galactic ALP dark-matter limit (90% CL) on g_Ae, red solid curve in Fig. 4, extracted from the vector figure Fig4GA_PandaXII.pdf in the arXiv e-print. Axes calibrated on tick labels (x: 1 and 10 keV/c^2; y: 1e-14..1e-10); masses converted keV->eV. Curve spans 1-25 keV/c^2, g_Ae ~ (0.6-4)e-13, consistent with the text statement g_Ae <~ 4e-13 over 1<mA<25 keV/c^2; the bump at 4-6 keV is the 127Xe background feature described in the text. Paper assumes local DM density rho=0.3 GeV/cm^3 (Eq. for Phi_A). The paper also reports a solar CBRD axion limit (~4e-13, flat for mA<1 keV/c^2) and a 57Fe 14.4 keV solar axion limit (Fig. 3); the galactic ALP result is chosen as it is the DM search the paper highlights as the strongest constraint to date.",
